<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Central and Southern Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Kwanyama Kingdom</h1><p class="st-meta">1700 CE – 1917 CE (approx.) · capital Ondjiva</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The largest Ovambo kingdom, straddling the Angola–Namibia border, whose last king Mandume ya Ndemufayo fought both Portugal and South Africa.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Oukwanyama formed by the 18th century on the floodplains around the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kunene-river">Kunene</a> and Cuvelai rivers, under kings drawn from a royal matriclan. It grew into the most populous of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ovambo-people">Ovambo</a> kingdoms, with its royal seat in the area of modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ondjiva">Ondjiva</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Kings held wide power over land and justice, ruling through district headmen and maintaining armed retainers. The economy combined <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/millet">millet</a> farming, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cattle">cattle</a>, salt and iron, and in the 19th century the kingdom traded cattle and captives for guns and horses with Portuguese and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boers">Boer</a> traders. German and Finnish missionaries worked in the kingdom from the 1880s.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mandume-ya-ndemufayo">Mandume ya Ndemufayo</a>, king from 1911, resisted Portuguese advances, but after the Portuguese victory at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-mongua">Mongua</a> in 1915 he withdrew south. He was killed fighting South African forces in 1917, and the kingdom was divided between <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/portuguese-angola">Portuguese Angola</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/south-west-africa">South West Africa</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 1700 CE – 1917 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Central and Southern Africa</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:93.53%;width:4.32%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1700 CE – 1917 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Ondjiva</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Mandume ya Ndemufayo</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Traditional Ovambo religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Oshikwanyama</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/angola">Angola</a>, <a href="/countries/namibia">Namibia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Oukwanyama, Uukwanyama</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1808&amp;focus=kwanyama-kingdom" aria-label="Kwanyama Kingdom on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5108 2811 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kwanyama Kingdom lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5428 3067L5366 2764M5428 3067L5457 3267"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5366 2764h0M5457 3267h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5428 3067h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5428 3067h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Ondjiva. <a href="/atlas?year=1808&amp;focus=kwanyama-kingdom">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

